Contamination creates major economic barriers to material recycling where recovery equipment becomes damaged or material quality becomes unrecyclable. Single incompatible components contaminate entire product streams, often making entire batches unrecyclable. Preventing contamination at design stage resolves economics of recycling viability.

Contaminant prevention reduces sorting labour intensity and equipment damage. Clean material streams enable economical recycling and higher recovered material value. Contamination-free design demonstrates commitment to recycling integrity.